# Figures and tables

- **Figures** carry one idea. Draw in `\sffamily`. Keep captions short: do not restate numbers already on the graphic.
- **Tables** are routes, inventories, or comparisons. Do not recast a correspondence diagram (e.g. Curry--Howard) as a numbered table; leave it a figure.
- **Main text** only needs the figures the argument uses. An appendix may repeat a graph if the local definition is opaque without it; the caption should name the main-text figure it matches.
- **Every figure and table** is `\cref`'d from the argument or explicitly introduced in the sentence that precedes it. A caption pointing at a definition does not replace that introduction.
- Mira endogenous nodes share circle style (`\sffamily`, `inner sep`, fill, arrow tips). Observed SCM drawings (5.2, A.1) stay `\small` / 8 mm; explicit-latent drawings (A.3, A.4) stay `\scriptsize` / 7 mm with rectangular exogenous roots.
